cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "empirica-networks: neighbour-limited visibility for Empirica experiments"
message: >-
  If you use this software in research, please cite it. A methods paper is in
  preparation (see PUBLICATION-PLAN.md); until it exists, cite the software.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Feltham
    given-names: Eric Martin
    email: eric.feltham@aya.yale.edu
# TODO: set once the repository has a remote — there is none as of 2026-08-16,
# and a plausible-looking URL that 404s is worse than an absent field.
# repository-code: "https://github.com/…/empirica-networks"
abstract: >-
  Network experiments for Empirica. Participants are nodes in a graph and each
  receives only their neighbours' projected state — enforced at the wire rather
  than in the interface, and verifiable with a shipped command that injects
  sentinel values and checks raw frames. Includes topology generators, rewiring
  during play, neighbour-scoped chat, seeded and reproducible realisation, and
  export helpers that run offline.
keywords:
  - empirica
  - network experiments
  - social networks
  - behavioural experiments
  - experimental design
license: MIT
version: 0.0.0
